sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Agent execution
  participant F as Sandbox and<br/>Credential Proxy
  participant C as OCC and<br/>credential custody
  participant G as GitHub

  Note over F,C: Before release: bind the execution, supervisor<br/>installation, and enforced policy
  Note over C,G: OCE prepares the scoped token<br/>in the background, not on request

  A-->>F: Read repository metadata
  Note over A,F: Pin the originating execution and response path at acceptance
  F-->>C: 1. Authorize this execution and actual read
  C-->>F: Resolve only an eligible committed token
  F-->>C: 2. Authorize that read and selected token version
  C-->>F: Record dispatch attempt, permit one send
  Note over F,C: Stale origin, unavailable authority, or ambiguous commit: no send

  F-->>G: Send the read with GitHub authentication
  G-->>F: Bounded response
  F-->>A: Approved response to original execution
